{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And all that go on their paws.</b> Rashi explained: such as a bear, a dog, and a cat — they certainly have split hooves, but they are forbidden on account of going on their paws. If so, investigation is needed regarding the shafan and the arnevet: why did Scripture forbid them on account of not having split hooves? It should have forbidden them on account of going on their paws."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:58.888272559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}